<p>Hello everyone!</p>
<p>My name is Lukas and I'm from germany. I first discovered the site many years ago, when I watched some YouTube creepypasta videos. I thought the idea of this wiki was fascinating and continued to go down the rabbit hole of this website.</p>
<p>I probably want to contribute to the site by voting (of course) and actually writing some articles. I had an idea for a SCP for quite some time now, but after reading some documents on this site, I want to give it some more time, since my idea seems to be one hard to write about (it's a supernatural humanoid). Also, my punctuation is more of a work-in-progress at this point in time. However, I am certain i can improve. I will also need to learn the proper coding for the Wikidot syntax.</p>
<p>Well, no matter how long it will take for me to publish my first article, I will certainly be on the lookout for new SCPs and opportunities to give new and old writers some good-hearted critique/feedback.</p>
<p>I am looking forward to working with you all!</p>
<p>P.S.: For the question of the month, I think I have to go with water. I'm normally very still, but a single drop will bring me into motion. If the motion is good or bad?&#8230; Well, only time will tell. After all, it depends on where the waves will move me.</p>

