<p>I'm not sure if I'm supposed to have separate threads for my tale and my scp article if the tale is about the scp. But I realized I didn't explain what happens in my first tale.</p>
<p>Edit to Central Narrative: The tale is about a man who come into a western town after being robbed and has essentially nothing. Then he meets a strange man in a bar who loves gambling, buys him dinner and drinks, and talks about his lucky coin. The two spend the night drinking and betting on coin flips with each other until sunrise. As they're watching sunrise we learn the man with nothing is a wanted man and the strange man forces him to make a bet on a flip of the coin. If he wins the man with nothing can have the strange man's horse and get out of town, if he loses the strange man can turn him in for the bounty. But on this flip the coin lands on its anomalous side, transforming the strange man into the monster, which then attacks the man with nothing.</p>
<p>The monster is a transformed version of whoever flips the coin, but they grow bigger and gain spikes on their head, extra pointy teeth and have long arms with boney scythes where their hands should be.</p>

